#HSSS 1.0
TITLE: Ubuntu White Edition / base-passwd Specification
PACKAGE: base-passwd
LANGUAGE: C, data, packaging
STATUS: W0/W1
ROLE: Foundational system users and groups

## PROGRAM
base-passwd provides the canonical baseline passwd/group identities expected by the Debian/Ubuntu system.

## STRUCTURE
SOURCE: upstream Ubuntu/Debian package
BOUNDARY: account/group definitions -> service ownership -> filesystem permissions
WHITE_EDITION: controlled identity review

## SPEC
- preserve established UID/GID compatibility
- add identities only for a documented service consumer
- apply least privilege
- keep account databases reproducible

## QUALITY
TEST: build, passwd/group verification, UID/GID compatibility, ownership review, upgrade test

## SOURCE POLICY
Do not add accounts for convenience. Native changes require a concrete service requirement and permission analysis.
